\noindent \textbf{Note:} All numbers must be regenerated from the actual training run. Report only empirically produced metrics.

\section{Observations}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Linear SVM achieves near-optimal accuracy on TF-IDF features with sub-millisecond latency, ideal for real-time applications.
    \item DistilBERT achieves the highest accuracy but requires $\sim$10$\times$ more inference time and $\sim$100$\times$ more training time.
    \item Naive Bayes serves as a fast, interpretable baseline.
    \item MLP sits between SVM and DistilBERT in both accuracy and speed.
\end{itemize}

